<title>GERMANY: Buba's Krupp - EMU criterion need not be exactly met.</title>
<headline>Buba's Krupp - EMU criterion need not be exactly met.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nations seeking to qualify for European monetary union do not need to hit the EMU debt criterion exactly to qualify, Bundesbank council member Hans-Juergen Krupp said on Monday.</p>
<p>Speaking at a savings bank meeting in Hamburg, the president of the Hamburg, Mecklenburg-Vorpommern and Schleswig-Holstein central bank said there would be room to manoeuvre, particularly in the area of public debt.</p>
<p>&quot;The 60-percent debt-to-GDP ratio is barely justifiable on grounds of economic theory, as (the debt) is above all a product of historical developments,&quot; said Krupp.</p>
</text>
